/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  column09_tray_hydraulics  --  column01, asked the question a converged MESH
  solution never answers: CAN THE TRAYS PASS THE TRAFFIC?

  A converged column tells you what separates.  It says nothing about whether
  the vapour rising through the holes will carry the liquid up with it
  (entrainment flooding), whether the liquid will back up the downcomer until
  it reaches the tray above (downcomer flooding), or whether it will simply
  rain through the holes instead of bubbling (weeping).  A column that floods
  separates nothing, and the stage equations never notice.

  Add an `hydraulics {}` block and the column runs a RATING pass on its own
  converged profile.  Two modes, the same equations in opposite directions:

    * give `diameter` -> RATING.  How close to flood is each tray?
    * omit `diameter` -> DESIGN.  What diameter keeps every tray at or below
                         `floodFraction` of its flooding velocity?  The widest
                         tray sets the column.  That is this case.

  Nothing here is guessed.  The orifice coefficient C_o is a chart in the
  literature (Liebson, Kelley & Bullington 1957, against hole-area ratio and
  plate-thickness/hole-diameter); it is a DECLARED number you own, printed back
  at you.  The weep-point constant K2 is a chart too -- leave it out and the
  column tells you the weep check was not performed rather than inventing it.

  Read the printed table.  The feed enters two-phase (370 K, 1 atm, 70 %
  vapour), so the vapour part joins the vapour traffic and the liquid part
  the liquid traffic: L rises across the feed (0.0278<!--golden: kpi column09 L_rect--> -> 0.0362<!--golden: kpi column09 L_strip--> kmol/s) and V
  FALLS (0.0417<!--golden: kpi column09 V_rect--> -> 0.0223<!--golden: kpi column09 V_strip--> kmol/s).  The flow parameter F_LV therefore
  jumps across the feed (0.041 on tray 7, 0.099 on tray 8), which lowers
  Fair's capacity parameter and with it the flooding velocity (1.53 -> 1.38
  m/s), but the vapour velocity falls much faster (1.22 -> 0.66 m/s).  So the
  RECTIFYING trays are the tight ones here: the flood approach climbs from
  74.4 % on the top tray to 80.0 %<!--golden: kpi column09 floodApproach_max *100--> on stage 7, just above the feed, and
  drops to 47-50 % on the stripping trays.  Stage 7 sets the 1.222 m<!--golden: kpi column09 diameter-->
  tower (the stripping section alone would need 0.969 m<!--golden: kpi column09 diameter_stripping-->, 20.7 % less),
  with a column pressure drop of 12.59 kPa<!--golden: kpi column09 dP_column_kPa--> and a downcomer backup of at most
  199.9 mm<!--golden: kpi column09 downcomerBackup_max_mm-->.

  (Header re-read 2026-11-25 against the engine's own run.  It had described a
  saturated-liquid feed, L doubling across it with V unchanged, a flood
  approach climbing to 80.0 % on stage 14 and a 1.316 m tower; the feed file is
  370 K at 70 % vapour and the run gives the numbers above.  The same stale
  paragraph had been "corrected" on 2026-09-07 against a printed table of the
  liquid-feed column, which is why it survived.)
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        column09;
        type        distillationColumn;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( distillate  bottoms );

        operation
        {
            nStages        15;
            feedStage      8;
            refluxRatio    2.0;
            distillateRate 50.0 kmol/h;
            P              1.01325 bar;

            hydraulics
            {
                trayType               sieve;
                // diameter            1.2;      // uncomment -> RATING mode
                traySpacing            0.50;     // m
                weirHeight             0.050;    // m
                holeDiameter           5.0e-3;   // m
                holeAreaFraction       0.10;     // A_holes / A_active
                downcomerAreaFraction  0.12;     // A_downcomer / A_tower
                weirLengthFraction     0.77;     // l_weir / D  (goes with 0.12)
                orificeCoefficient     0.84;     // C_o -- read off the Liebson chart
                floodFraction          0.80;     // design target
                K2                     30.7;     // weep chart at h_w + h_ow ~ 60 mm
            }
        }

        compositionTol   1e-7;
        maxOuterIter     200;
    }
);
